# name: test/sql/copy/csv/test_block_scan_skip_runs_dialects.test
# description: Runs of unprojected columns skipped with one call in multi-byte delimiter, CR, CRLF and comment dialects, results, errors and rejects stay the same
# group: [csv]

# the fixtures depend on exact byte offsets
require notwindows

# Every block_scan_runs_*.csv holds the rows of block_scan_runs.csv written with the dialect: 12 columns, a tab, a quoted
# value holding the delimiter, a quote in an unquoted value, a space before a quote, empty values, too few and too many
# columns, an escaped quote, a run across a block edge, a multi-byte delimiter across a block edge and no newline after
# the last row; the multi-byte delimiter files add a partial match of the delimiter inside a value, the comment files
# comment lines, a comment byte inside a value and a comment byte right after a delimiter. Projections leave runs of
# unprojected columns on both sides of the 6 columns from which a run is skipped with one call. Expected results are
# those of a build without the run skipping.

# file pipe2, strict, counting
statement error
SELECT count(*) FROM read_csv('{DATA_DIR}/csv/block_scan_runs_pipe2.csv', delim='||', new_line='\n', quote='"', escape='"', header=false, auto_detect=false, columns={'a':'INTEGER','b':'VARCHAR','c':'VARCHAR','d':'VARCHAR','e':'VARCHAR','f':'VARCHAR','g':'VARCHAR','h':'VARCHAR','i':'VARCHAR','j':'VARCHAR','k':'VARCHAR','l':'VARCHAR'})
----
Invalid Input Error: CSV Error on Line: 7

